    "module Bitwise\n"
    + "\n"
    + "(** Bitwise operations on integers, and the constraint behind `band`, `bor`,\n"
    + "    `bxor`, and `bnot`. Every instance computes the true integer answer: two's\n"
    + "    complement over integers of unbounded width, so an `Int` and a `BigInt`\n"
    + "    holding the same value give the same answer. The standard instances are\n"
    + "    `Int` and `BigInt`. *)\n"
    + "export constraint Bitwise<a> =\n"
    + "    (** Each bit of the result is set where it is set in both `left` and\n"
    + "        `right`. The operator `band` spells it. *)\n"
    + "    bitAnd(left: a, right: a) -> a\n"
    + "    (** Each bit of the result is set where it is set in `left` or `right`.\n"
    + "        The operator `bor` spells it. *)\n"
    + "    bitOr(left: a, right: a) -> a\n"
    + "    (** Each bit of the result is set where exactly one of `left` and `right`\n"
    + "        has it set. The operator `bxor` spells it. *)\n"
    + "    bitXor(left: a, right: a) -> a\n"
    + "    (** Every bit of `value` flipped, which is `-value - 1`. The operator\n"
    + "        `bnot` spells it. *)\n"
    + "    bitNot(value: a) -> a\n"
    + "    (** `value` times two to the power `count`. A negative `count` shifts\n"
