    + "// which is the shape the member has (#541). Every exponent and scale here is an\n"
    + "// `Int` counter for that reason: the magnitudes stay under about 1100, far\n"
    + "// inside the safe range, and the only thing that ever needs to be a `BigInt` is\n"
    + "// the value being shifted. Nothing crosses into `Float` until the final\n"
    + "// assembly, which is why the rounding happens once.\n"
    + "\n"
    + "// The number of binary digits in a positive `value`: the unique `n` with\n"
    + "// `2 ** (n - 1) <= value < 2 ** n`. A doubling search finds a bound and a\n"
    + "// bisection closes on it, so the cost is logarithmic in the answer rather than\n"
    + "// linear in it — the exponents here reach into the thousands.\n"
