    + "//\n"
    + "// The type row declares `Vector` itself (`spec/intrinsics.md` section 3.3): the\n"
    + "// type is this module's own, its values are the runtime's `TrieVector` records,\n"
    + "// and the `+` is checked against that record's variance here, at the row.\n"
    + "extern from \"hex:intrinsic\"\n"
    + "    (** An ordered list of elements of one type, written `[10, 20, 30]`.\n"
    + "        Positions count from 1, so `items[1]` is the first element. A vector\n"
    + "        never changes: functions such as `append` and `set` return a new vector\n"
    + "        and leave the original as it was. A new vector made by adding or\n"
